      "raw": "I just want to say if you only play the Sentenels Video game you might want to check out my related topic here before reading this one.\n\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/app/337150/discussions/0/1368380934244754312/\n\n<br /><br />So I just finished my first game of Villains of the multiverse (Ranatic, Scholar, Guise, and&nbsp; Bunker vs Greazer, Sergeant Steel, Miss Information, and Biomancer). After a close win (Biomancer did not want to die but Scholar eventually put him down) I started my usual post using a new deck ritual of going through all the cards, seeing the ones that I missed and reading the little comic on each. Now during the game Sergeant Steel had gotten a rather raw deal. First Fanatic had End of Days away his whole team, and then she had used Wrathful Retribution on him at 1 hp basically one shotting him so he never really got a chance to show off any of his stuff.<br /><br />The first thing that caught my eye was his birth place, New York, New York. Like me. Hey I already feel a connection to this guy! The first card listed was Arsonator and his little comic mentions how he doesn&#39;t speak much because his lungs don&#39;t work. &quot;Hey just like the Pyro in Team Fortress 2&quot; I think to myself. Next card is the Battle Medic. &quot;Hey a battle medic *thinking pause* just like in Team Fortress 2? Hey wait a minute.&quot; So I look at all his cards at once and begin to see more and more familiar faces. I count up the number of Agents and sure enough there are 9 (counting Sergeant Steel) and each one of them is a mirror of the 9 mercenaries (playable characters) from Team fortress 2. Coincidence? Maybe but the resemblance is so blatent that I&#39;m sure it couldn&#39;t be so I begin to search teh internets to see if I could get confirmation.<br /><br />Although there is nothing on the Wiki about the reference there is one topic on BGG where someone else noticed the resemblance too:<br />https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/1516951/sergeant-steel<br /><br />So then I searched this site for the word Team Fortress and would you look at what I found:<br />https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/team-fortress-2<br /><br />I don&#39;t know about you but it seems pretty compelling to me  :sunglasses: ",
